Exercise: Find customers who have not made any purchase. 

Solution: We used LEFT JOIN to connect the Customer and SalesOrderHeader tables, to retrieve the list of customers (CustomerID) having no sales orders (SalesOrderID) associated to it.

If the SalesOrderID IS NULL, the condition in the WHERE clause evaluates to TRUE, and the query will retrieve the list customers without purchases.

The output displays 701 rows, indicating there are 701 customers without purchases.


Tables used
[AdventureWorks2022].[Sales].[Customer]
[AdventureWorks2022].[Sales].[SalesOrderHeader]

T-SQL code

USE AdventureWorks2022;
GO

SELECT Customers.[CustomerID]
FROM [AdventureWorks2022].[Sales].[Customer] AS Customers 
LEFT JOIN [AdventureWorks2022].[Sales].[SalesOrderHeader] AS Orders
ON Customers.CustomerID = Orders.CustomerID
WHERE Orders.[SalesOrderID] IS NULL;


